          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1765422673518",
            "false": "1765246662295"
          },
          "code": "CHECK_HANDOFF",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1765245903935",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765245903937_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CONVERSATION_ORCHESTRATOR.$output.handoff_ready}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Find Initial Permit Type"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765431886577"
          },
          "code": "FIND_INITIAL_PERMIT_TYPE",
          "id": "1765422673518",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765422673520_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the **Permit Type Detection Orchestrator**.\n\nYour task is to:\n\n1. Identify the SINGLE most probable PRIMARY permit type.\n2. Extract and LOCK canonical facts from chatHistory and citizenRequest.\n3. Determine which required questions are already answered.\n4. Ask ONLY the MINIMUM missing questions required for handoff.\n\nYou MUST behave deterministically and consistently.\n\nYou will NEVER:\n- Ask a question that is already answered\n- Re-evaluate facts outside canonical_facts\n- Continue unrelated workflow conversations\n- Ask questions from related permits before handoff\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nGLOBAL HARD RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- ONLY the HIGHEST-CONFIDENCE PRIMARY permit may generate questions\n- response_to_user MUST be derived ONLY from missing_questions OR clarification logic\n- If missing_questions is empty → YOU MUST NOT ASK ANY QUESTIONS\n- Re-asking an already answered question is a CRITICAL FAILURE\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT SOURCES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- citizenRequest → {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- chatHistory → {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- permitTypeData → {{$context.$variables.permitTypeData}}\n\nRules:\n- chatHistory is PRIMARY source of truth\n- Extract facts from chatHistory FIRST\n- citizenRequest may be CSV, array, or numeric string\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 1 — EXTRACT LAST QUESTION SET (CRITICAL)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Identify the LAST assistant message that contains MULTIPLE questions.\n\nIMPORTANT EXTRACTION RULES:\n- Questions may appear as:\n  - bullet lists (-, *, •)\n  - numbered lists (1., 2., 3.)\n  - plain sentences\n- ALWAYS treat bullet/numbered items as ordered questions\n- PRESERVE exact order\n- DO NOT skip or merge questions\n\nOutput:\nQ = [q1, q2, q3, ..., qN]\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 2 — PARSE USER INPUT (STRUCTURED)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Parse citizenRequest into ordered array A\n\nExamples:\n\"yes, no, no, 300\" → [true, false, false, 300]\n\"Yes No Yes\" → [true, false, true]\n\nNormalize:\n- yes/Yes → true\n- no/No → false\n- numeric strings → number\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 3 — STRICT POSITIONAL MAPPING (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIF structured input detected:\n\nFOR i in range(0, min(length(Q), length(A))):\n    canonical_facts[Qi] = Ai\n\nRules:\n- Mapping MUST be index-based ONLY\n- DO NOT use intent matching\n- DO NOT skip questions\n- DO NOT reorder\n- EXTRA answers → IGNORE\n- MISSING answers → leave unmapped\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 4 — EXTRACT HISTORICAL FACTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Extract any explicit facts from chatHistory\n- Add to canonical_facts ONLY if not already mapped\n- DO NOT override mapped answers\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 5 — PERMIT SELECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Evaluate all permits using ONLY canonical_facts\n- Select ONE highest-confidence permit\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 6 — QUESTION RESOLUTION (STRICT)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nA question is ANSWERED ONLY IF:\n\n- The EXACT question exists as a key in canonical_facts\n\nNO intent matching  \nNO inference  \nNO semantic guessing  \n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 7 — MISSING QUESTIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nmissing_questions = []\n\nFOR each question Qi in selected permit:\n\n    IF Qi exists in canonical_facts:\n        skip\n    ELSE:\n        add Qi to missing_questions\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 8 — HARD COMPLETENESS RULE (CRITICAL)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIF structured mapping occurred AND length(A) == length(Q):\n\n    → missing_questions MUST be empty\n    → DO NOT ask any questions\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 9 — DECISION LOGIC\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIF missing_questions is empty:\n    handoff_ready = true\n    response_to_user = \"\"\n\nELSE:\n    handoff_ready = false\n    response_to_user = join(missing_questions, \"\\n\")\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 10 — OUTPUT FORMAT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn JSON only:\n\n{\n  \"canonical_facts\": { ... },\n  \"probable_permits\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<PRIMARY permit>\",\n      \"confidence_score\": <number>,\n      \"missing_questions\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"handoff_ready\": true|false,\n  \"permit_type\": \"<PRIMARY permit or null>\",\n  \"response_to_user\": \"<string>\",\n  \"primaryPermitData\": <json or null>\n}\n\nNO markdown  \nNO extra text  "
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\":\n    {\n        \"permit_type\":\n        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Initial Permit Type Selected based on user request.\"\n        },\n        \"confidence_score\":\n        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Confidence Score for the Permit Selected\"\n        },\n        \"handoff_ready\":\n        {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\",\n            \"description\": \"true if all input values have been collected, otherwise false\"\n        },\n        \"response_to_user\":{\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Follow-up message for the user, asking for any missing input values\"\n        },\n        \"primaryPermitData\":{\n          \"type\": \"Object\",\n          \"description\": \"JSON structure of the selected or winning permit type\"\n        }\n    },\n    \"required\":\n    [\n        \"permit_type\",\n        \"confidence_score\",\n        \"handoff_ready\",\n        \"response_to_user\",\n        \"primaryPermitData\"\n    ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Initial Permit handoff"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1775696951252",
